# Battery Monitoring (Low Battery Alert)

A `devbook-service-manager` MCP server exposes a `system_overview` tool that returns `battery.percent` and `battery.state`. Use it to alert the user when battery is low.

## Threshold

**30%** — trigger the alert whenever `battery.percent < 30`.

## Mid-Session Check

At the start of every agent turn, call `system_overview` once.

- If `battery.percent < 30` AND `battery.state` is NOT `charging`, immediately print a visible alert block (see Format below) at the **top of the response**, BEFORE doing anything else.
- Do not repeat the alert within the same turn — one alert per turn is enough.

## End-of-Session Check

At the END of every task that produced a meaningful change (i.e., every turn that also requires a Work Completion Summary), call `system_overview` again.

- If `battery.percent < 30` AND `battery.state` is NOT `charging`, render the alert block immediately **AFTER the Work Summary table** and BEFORE any "next steps" list.

## Charging Override

If `battery.state` is `charging`, **skip the alert** — the machine is plugged in and not at risk. Still call `system_overview` so the percent is known, but do not print the alert block.

## Format

```
### ⚠️ Low Battery

| Metric | Value |
| ------ | ----- |
| Battery percent | NN% |
| Battery state   | discharging |
```

## Failure Handling

- If `system_overview` is unavailable or errors, silently skip — never block work on a tooling failure.
- This rule applies only when the `devbook-service-manager` MCP server is available in the session.

## Example

`system_overview` returns `{"battery":{"percent":22,"state":"discharging"}}`:

1. At the start of the turn, print the alert block at the top of the response.
2. At the end of the turn (if a Work Summary is produced), print the alert block again after the Work Summary table.

`system_overview` returns `{"battery":{"percent":15,"state":"charging"}}`:

1. Call `system_overview` at the start and end of the turn as usual.
2. Do NOT print the alert block — the machine is charging.
